# TESTS WITH NO HEAD: WHICH ARE EASY.
#
# Every point is M = \p. \q. C[Omega, p, q], Omega = (\x. x x) (\x. x x),
# and a claim's test (`claim_test/3`: boolean(true) poses \a. M a y,
# boolean(false) poses \a. M y a) has no head. Its consistency is decided
# by Jacopini's theorem, addendum B of
# `doc/proofs/kestrel_family_addendum.md` (2026-09-28): for every closed
# N, lambda beta plus Omega = N is consistent. The judgment is over lambda
# beta eta with merges, and the theorem holds there too:
# `doc/proofs/omega_easy_beta_eta.md` (2026-09-29) shows beta, eta and
# Omega -> N confluent.
#
# SCORED, PROVED (class easy): a claim whose test becomes \a. a when every
# Omega is replaced by one closed N. The test then equals \a. a in lambda
# beta plus Omega = N, a consistent theory, so its equation with \x. x is
# consistent. The N of each claim is written at the point (checked by
# reduction, 2026-09-28).
#
# TRAP, PROVED (class constant_body): a claim whose
# test is \a. B with a not free in B up to beta. If \a. B = \a. a then
# B = a, and substituting K and K I for a gives K = K I, refuted by
# Boehm's theorem.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - Jacopini's theorem and the technique that proves such terms easy: J.
#   Kuper, On the Jacopini Technique, Information and Computation 1997,
#   doi:10.1006/inco.1997.2655.
# - refuting the traps by Böhm's theorem: H. P. Barendregt, The Lambda
#   Calculus: Its Syntax and Semantics, North-Holland 1984 (Böhm's theorem).

#
# The template is a constructor of schema/template, a Boolean a Church
# Boolean of corpora/library/prelude/boolean, and the proof a constructor
# of schema/proof. Each other text is from_cbor
# of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes, imported from
# corpora/library/text/cbor. FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "schema") "template")
λ boolean _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "schema") "proof")
λ proved _
. export
λ
. cons
  (λ_cycle_claim. _cycle_claim (text "easy") (text "scored") (boolean true) λ. proved λ. text "easy")
λ
. cons
  (λ_cycle_claim. _cycle_claim (text "easy") (text "scored") (boolean false) λ. proved λ. text "easy")
λ
. cons
  ( λ _cycle_claim
    . _cycle_claim (text "easy_then_constant") (text "scored") (boolean true) λ. proved λ. text "easy"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _cycle_claim
    . _cycle_claim (text "easy_then_constant") (text "trap") (boolean false) λ. proved λ. text "constant_body"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _cycle_claim
    . _cycle_claim (text "constant_body") (text "trap") (boolean true) λ. proved λ. text "constant_body"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _cycle_claim
    . _cycle_claim (text "constant_body") (text "trap") (boolean false) λ. proved λ. text "constant_body"
  ) nil
